R538	Cueing Arg1:T384 Arg2:T386	
R539	Speaker Arg1:T385 Arg2:T386	
T387	Entity 36891 36893	us
R540	Addressee Arg1:T387 Arg2:T383	
R541	Addressee Arg1:T387 Arg2:T386	
T388	Quotation 38890 38909	"Your French gold?"
R542	Addressee Arg1:T385 Arg2:T388	
R543	Speaker Arg1:T337 Arg2:T388	
T389	Quotation 38910 39404	"Yes. We had occasion some months ago to strengthen our resources and borrowed for that purpose 30,000 napoleons from the Bank of France. It has become known that we have never had occasion to unpack the money, and that it is still lying in our cellar. The crate upon which I sit contains 2,000 napoleons packed between layers of lead foil. Our reserve of bullion is much larger at present than is usually kept in a single branch office, and the directors have had misgivings upon the subject."
R544	Speaker Arg1:T385 Arg2:T389	
R545	Addressee Arg1:T337 Arg2:T389	
T390	Quotation 39405 39438	"Which were very well justified,"
T391	Cue 39439 39447	observed
T392	Entity 39448 39454	Holmes
R546	Cueing Arg1:T391 Arg2:T390	
R547	Speaker Arg1:T392 Arg2:T390	
R548	Addressee Arg1:T385 Arg2:T390	
T393	Quotation 39456 39650	"And now it is time that we arranged our little plans. I expect that within an hour matters will come to a head. In the meantime Mr. Merryweather, we must put the screen over that dark lantern."
R549	Speaker Arg1:T392 Arg2:T393	
R550	Cueing Arg1:T391 Arg2:T393	
R551	Addressee Arg1:T385 Arg2:T393	
T394	Quotation 39651 39673	"And sit in the dark?"
R552	Addressee Arg1:T392 Arg2:T394	
R553	Speaker Arg1:T385 Arg2:T394	
T395	Quotation 39674 40292	"I am afraid so. I had brought a pack of cards in my pocket, and I thought that, as we were a partie carrée, you might have your rubber after all. But I see that the enemy's preparations have gone so far that we cannot risk the presence of a light. And, first of all, we must choose our positions. These are daring men, and though we shall take them at a disadvantage, they may do us some harm unless we are careful. I shall stand behind this crate, and do you conceal yourselves behind those. Then, when I flash a light upon them, close in swiftly. If they fire, Watson, have no compunction about shooting them down."
R554	Speaker Arg1:T392 Arg2:T395	
R555	Addressee Arg1:T385 Arg2:T395	
T396	Entity 40293 40294	I
R556	Addressee Arg1:T396 Arg2:T395	
T397	Quotation 40808 40836	"They have but one retreat,"
T398	Cue 40837 40846	whispered
